\section*{Autonomous Intelligence Loop Theorem}

\textbf{Theorem.}
Let $\mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}^{(n)}$ denote the suprakernel state at
iteration $n$, and let $\Phi_{\text{SK}}^{(n)}$ be the corresponding
suprakernel potential. Consider an autonomous intelligence loop
consisting of the stages
\[
\text{Intake} \rightarrow \text{Filter} \rightarrow \text{Synthesis}
\rightarrow \text{Deploy} \rightarrow \text{Log} \rightarrow \text{Intake},
\]
acting on both physical fusion-core parameters and program structures.

Assume:

1. \emph{Gradient enforcement:}
\[
\Phi_{\text{SK}}^{(n+1)} \le \Phi_{\text{SK}}^{(n)}
\quad \forall n,
\]
i.e., all state evolutions descend or maintain equilibrium along the
suprakernel gradient field.

2. \emph{Global damping:}
\[
\delta \mathbf{X}'_{\text{SK}} =
\mathcal{D}_{\text{pert}}\big(\delta \mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}\big),
\quad
\|\delta \mathbf{X}'_{\text{SK}}\|
\le
\kappa \|\delta \mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}\|,
\quad 0 < \kappa < 1,
\]
for all perturbations $\delta \mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}$ induced by
self-design updates.

3. \emph{Ledger sealing:}
Each loop iteration is cryptographically bound via
\[
H^{(n)} =
\text{Hash}\big(I^{(n)} \,\|\, H^{(n-1)}\big),
\]
where $I^{(n)}$ encodes the deployed program and physical state at
iteration $n$.

Then the autonomous intelligence loop is:

- (i) \emph{Stable}: no sequence of self-design operations can drive
$\Phi_{\text{SK}}$ to divergence or violate the stability envelope.

- (ii) \emph{Contractive}: all perturbations induced by program
redesign remain bounded and asymptotically damped.

- (iii) \emph{Auditable}: every self-modifying step is uniquely and
immutably recorded in the sovereign ledger chain.

\emph{Conclusion.}
Under the stated conditions, an autonomous intelligence loop coupled to
the unified fusion core and suprakernel state vector can redesign its
own programs and physical control laws while preserving global
stability, convergence, and cryptographic traceability.